{"id":"a28bcf113a6c9da0","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-thm-weyl-law.md","title":"Weyl Law for the Dirichlet Laplacian","display":"thm-weyl-law — Weyl Law for the Dirichlet Laplacian","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-weyl-law","aliases":["58-thm-weyl-law"],"display":"thm-weyl-law — Weyl Law for the Dirichlet Laplacian","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-weyl-law"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-weyl-law</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-weyl-law — Weyl Law for the Dirichlet Laplacian"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"efadc4e149119d7f\" href=\"?note=efadc4e149119d7f\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md\">../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|&lt;1\\}\">\\(B_n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|&lt;1\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathrm{Euc}}^n\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathrm{Euc}}^n\\)</span> is the standard Euclidean topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S\\)</span> are explicitly defined below.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)\">\\(\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)\\)</span> is the Euclidean Laplacian predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"efadc4e149119d7f\" href=\"?note=efadc4e149119d7f\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md\">../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Vol}_n\">\\(\\operatorname{Vol}_n\\)</span> is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-dimensional Lebesgue volume.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}domain}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S(\\Omega,n)\n\\leftrightarrow\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\n\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\n\\land\\Omega\\in\\tau_{\\mathrm{Euc}}^n\n\\land\\exists R\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\Omega\\subseteq\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|&lt;R\\}\n\\land\\operatorname{Vol}_n(\\partial\\Omega)=0.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}domain}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S(\\Omega,n)\n\\leftrightarrow\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\n\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\n\\land\\Omega\\in\\tau_{\\mathrm{Euc}}^n\n\\land\\exists R\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\Omega\\subseteq\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|&lt;R\\}\n\\land\\operatorname{Vol}_n(\\partial\\Omega)=0.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dirichlet\\text{-}eigenbasis}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S(u,\\lambda_\\bullet;\\Omega,n,\\Delta_n)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land u\\in L^2(\\Omega)^\\omega\n\\land\\forall j,k\\in\\omega\\;\n(\\langle u_j,u_k\\rangle_{L^2(\\Omega)}=\\delta_{jk})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\overline{\\operatorname{span}\\{u_j:j\\in\\omega\\}}^{\\,L^2(\\Omega)}\n=L^2(\\Omega)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\lambda_\\bullet,\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall j\\in\\omega\\;\n\\bigl(u_j\\in H_0^1(\\Omega)\\cap C^\\infty(\\Omega)\n\\land-\\Delta_nu_j=\\lambda_\\bullet(j)u_j\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall j\\in\\omega\\;\n(\\lambda_\\bullet(j)\\leq\\lambda_\\bullet(j+1))\n\\land\\lim_{j\\to\\infty}\\lambda_\\bullet(j)=\\infty.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dirichlet\\text{-}eigenbasis}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S(u,\\lambda_\\bullet;\\Omega,n,\\Delta_n)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land u\\in L^2(\\Omega)^\\omega\n\\land\\forall j,k\\in\\omega\\;\n(\\langle u_j,u_k\\rangle_{L^2(\\Omega)}=\\delta_{jk})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\overline{\\operatorname{span}\\{u_j:j\\in\\omega\\}}^{\\,L^2(\\Omega)}\n=L^2(\\Omega)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\lambda_\\bullet,\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall j\\in\\omega\\;\n\\bigl(u_j\\in H_0^1(\\Omega)\\cap C^\\infty(\\Omega)\n\\land-\\Delta_nu_j=\\lambda_\\bullet(j)u_j\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall j\\in\\omega\\;\n(\\lambda_\\bullet(j)\\leq\\lambda_\\bullet(j+1))\n\\land\\lim_{j\\to\\infty}\\lambda_\\bullet(j)=\\infty.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weyl\\text{-}counting\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S(N,\\lambda_\\bullet)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Function}(N,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\nN(t)=|\\{j\\in\\omega:\\lambda_\\bullet(j)\\leq t\\}|.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weyl\\text{-}counting\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S(N,\\lambda_\\bullet)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Function}(N,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\nN(t)=|\\{j\\in\\omega:\\lambda_\\bullet(j)\\leq t\\}|.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}weyl\\text{-}law}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S(\\Omega,n)\n\\land\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S\n(u,\\lambda_\\bullet;\\Omega,n,\\Delta_n)\n\\land\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S(N,\\lambda_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\to\n\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}\\frac{N(t)}{t^{n/2}}\n=\n\\frac{\\operatorname{Vol}_n(B_n)\\operatorname{Vol}_n(\\Omega)}{(2\\pi)^n}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}weyl\\text{-}law}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S(\\Omega,n)\n\\land\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S\n(u,\\lambda_\\bullet;\\Omega,n,\\Delta_n)\n\\land\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S(N,\\lambda_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\to\n\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}\\frac{N(t)}{t^{n/2}}\n=\n\\frac{\\operatorname{Vol}_n(B_n)\\operatorname{Vol}_n(\\Omega)}{(2\\pi)^n}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The former dependency named “spectrum” described model cardinalities, not the spectrum of an operator, and therefore could not support Weyl's law.</li>\n<li>The domain hypothesis is expanded as bounded Euclidean openness with measure-zero boundary; this regularity suffices for the stated leading Weyl asymptotic.</li>\n<li>The eigenvalue sequence is tied to an explicitly complete orthonormal Dirichlet eigenbasis, so completeness and multiplicity are no longer hidden in an undeclared enumeration predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md","status":"resolved","id":"efadc4e149119d7f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md","status":"resolved","id":"efadc4e149119d7f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)$ is the Euclidean Laplacian predicate from [[../batch02/58-df-laplacian.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"B_n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|<1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathrm{Euc}}^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Vol}_n","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}smooth\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}domain}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S(\\Omega,n)\n\\leftrightarrow\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\n\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\n\\land\\Omega\\in\\tau_{\\mathrm{Euc}}^n\n\\land\\exists R\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\Omega\\subseteq\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|<R\\}\n\\land\\operatorname{Vol}_n(\\partial\\Omega)=0.","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dirichlet\\text{-}eigenbasis}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S(u,\\lambda_\\bullet;\\Omega,n,\\Delta_n)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Laplacian}_S(\\Delta_n,n)\\\\\n&{}\\land u\\in L^2(\\Omega)^\\omega\n\\land\\forall j,k\\in\\omega\\;\n(\\langle u_j,u_k\\rangle_{L^2(\\Omega)}=\\delta_{jk})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\overline{\\operatorname{span}\\{u_j:j\\in\\omega\\}}^{\\,L^2(\\Omega)}\n=L^2(\\Omega)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\lambda_\\bullet,\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall j\\in\\omega\\;\n\\bigl(u_j\\in H_0^1(\\Omega)\\cap C^\\infty(\\Omega)\n\\land-\\Delta_nu_j=\\lambda_\\bullet(j)u_j\\bigr)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall j\\in\\omega\\;\n(\\lambda_\\bullet(j)\\leq\\lambda_\\bullet(j+1))\n\\land\\lim_{j\\to\\infty}\\lambda_\\bullet(j)=\\infty.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weyl\\text{-}counting\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S(N,\\lambda_\\bullet)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Function}(N,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\nN(t)=|\\{j\\in\\omega:\\lambda_\\bullet(j)\\leq t\\}|.","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}weyl\\text{-}law}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{SmoothBoundedDomain}_S(\\Omega,n)\n\\land\\mathrm{DirichletEigenbasis}_S\n(u,\\lambda_\\bullet;\\Omega,n,\\Delta_n)\n\\land\\mathrm{CountingFunction}_S(N,\\lambda_\\bullet)\\\\\n&{}\\to\n\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}\\frac{N(t)}{t^{n/2}}\n=\n\\frac{\\operatorname{Vol}_n(B_n)\\operatorname{Vol}_n(\\Omega)}{(2\\pi)^n}.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":3051,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4488","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-thm-weyl-law.md|58-thm-weyl-law]]（batch10）"}],"outgoing":["efadc4e149119d7f","36d7463d215be751"]}